        "section": [
          {
            "text": {
              "status": "generated",
              "div": "<div xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1999/xhtml\">COPD exacerbation, treated with bronchodilators and steroids</div>"
            },
            "code": {
              "coding": [
                {
                  "code": "67781-5",
                  "system": "http://loinc.org",
                  "display": "Summarization of encounter note"
                }
              ]
            },
            "title": "Synthesis"
          },
          {
            "text": {
              "status": "generated",
              "div": "<div xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1999/xhtml\">Dear colleague, I am writing to inform you about the recent hospitalisation of your 84-year-old male patient, admitted on 29/07/2018 due to an acute exacerbation of his known chronic obstructive pulmonary disease (COPD). On admission, clinical examination revealed significant dyspnoea, reduced oxygen saturation, and diffuse expiratory wheezing. Chest X-ray confirmed hyperinflation without consolidation. Arterial blood gas analysis demonstrated hypoxaemic respiratory insufficiency. Blood tests showed mild systemic inflammation. The patient was treated with supplemental oxygen therapy, nebulised bronchodilators, systemic corticosteroids, and supportive intravenous fluids. Oxygen saturation was continuously monitored throughout the stay. The patient responded well to treatment with notable symptomatic improvement. He was discharged on 30/07/2018 on optimised inhaled therapy and a short course of oral steroids. I recommend close follow-up and pulmonary rehabilitation referral. Please do not hesitate to contact me for further information.</div>"
            },
            "code": {
